## 6. Sales Target Analysis

### 11. Sales Target

Example measure when a target column is available.

```dax
Sales Target =
SUM(Sales[Sales Target])
```

### 12. Sales Gap

Calculates the difference between actual sales and target sales.

```dax
Sales Gap =
[Total Revenue] - [Sales Target]
```

### 13. Target Achievement (%)

Calculates the percentage of the sales target achieved.

```dax
Target Achievement % =
DIVIDE(
    [Total Revenue],
    [Sales Target],
    0
) * 100
```

---

## 7. Customer Analysis Measures

### 14. Total Customers

Calculates the number of unique customers.

```dax
Total Customers =
DISTINCTCOUNT(Sales[Customer ID])
```

### 15. Returning Customers

Example calculation of customers with more than one distinct order.

```dax
Returning Customers =
COUNTROWS(
    FILTER(
        VALUES(Sales[Customer ID]),
        CALCULATE(
            DISTINCTCOUNT(Sales[Order ID])
        ) > 1
    )
)
```

### 16. Returning Customer Percentage

Calculates the percentage of customers who placed multiple orders.

```dax
Returning Customer % =
DIVIDE(
    [Returning Customers],
    [Total Customers],
    0
) * 100
```

